# Skill: Add Component

## When to use this skill

Use when creating a new React component — whether a UI primitive, a shared utility component, a feature-specific component, or a heavy client detail screen.

---

## Step 1 — Determine placement

Choose the correct directory based on the component's purpose:

| Directory | When to use |
|-----------|-------------|
| `src/components/ui/` | Only for shadcn/Radix UI generated primitives. No business logic. |
| `src/components/shared/` | Reusable display components used across multiple features (e.g. `Badge`, `EmptyState`, `Skeleton`, `Rating`) |
| `src/components/layout/` | Chrome — `Navbar`, `Footer`, `MobileTabBar` |
| `src/components/listing/` | Listing-specific UI (e.g. filters, map blur) |
| `src/components/listings/` | Heavy listing client screens (`ListingDetailClient`) |
| `src/components/admin/` | Admin dashboard UI (tables, modals) |
| `src/components/reviews/` | Review forms and lists |
| `src/components/roommate/` | Roommate filter components |
| `src/components/roommates/` | Heavy roommate client screens |
| `src/components/auth/` | Auth-specific UI (e.g. `EmailVerificationBanner`) |
| `src/components/providers/` | React context providers and guards — touch only if needed |

**Rule:** If a component is used in only one feature, put it in that feature's directory. If used across two or more features, it belongs in `shared/`.

---

## Step 2 — Write the component

### Base structure

```typescript
'use client'; // only if using hooks, browser APIs, or event handlers

import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';
// Radix/shadcn primitives from src/components/ui/
import { Card, CardContent } from '@/components/ui/card';
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
// Icons from lucide-react
import { Heart } from 'lucide-react';

interface MyComponentProps {
  title: string;
  className?: string;
}

export function MyComponent({ title, className }: MyComponentProps) {
  return (
    <Card className={cn('some-base-class', className)}>
      <CardContent>
        <Heart className='h-4 w-4' />
        <span>{title}</span>
      </CardContent>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

### Class merging

Always use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils.ts` (wraps `clsx` + `tailwind-merge`) when accepting a `className` prop or conditionally applying Tailwind classes:

```typescript
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

<div className={cn('base-class', isActive && 'active-class', className)}>
```

### Variants with CVA

For components with multiple visual variants, use `class-variance-authority`:

```typescript
import { cva, type VariantProps } from 'class-variance-authority';

const badgeVariants = cva('base-classes', {
  variants: {
    variant: {
      default: 'bg-primary text-primary-foreground',
      success: 'bg-green-500 text-white',
      secondary: 'bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground',
    },
  },
  defaultVariants: { variant: 'default' },
});

interface BadgeProps extends VariantProps<typeof badgeVariants> {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  className?: string;
}
```

See `src/components/shared/Badge.tsx` and `src/components/ui/badge.tsx` for examples.

