## Step 3 — Data fetching inside the component

If the component needs server data, use a TanStack Query hook from `src/hooks/api/`:

```typescript
import { useListings } from '@/hooks/api/useListings';

export function FeaturedListings() {
  const { data, isLoading, isError } = useListings({ status: 'available', sortBy: 'rating', limit: 6 });

  if (isLoading) return <LoadingSkeleton />;
  if (isError) return <ErrorState />;

  return <div>{data?.listings.map(l => <ListingCard key={l.id} listing={l} />)}</div>;
}
```

Never call `fetch()` or `axios` directly from a component. Never import from `src/lib/services/` or `src/lib/db/`.

---

## Step 4 — User feedback

For all async actions (save, submit, delete), use `sonner` toasts:

```typescript
import { toast } from 'sonner';

const mutation = useSaveListing();

const handleSave = async () => {
  try {
    await mutation.mutateAsync(listingId);
    toast.success('Listing saved');
  } catch (error) {
    toast.error(error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Failed to save listing');
  }
};
```

---

## Step 5 — Loading and empty states

Always handle three UI states:

```typescript
if (isLoading) {
  return (
    <div className='grid grid-cols-3 gap-4'>
      {[...Array(3)].map((_, i) => <Skeleton key={i} className='h-32 w-full' />)}
    </div>
  );
}

if (isError || !data) {
  return <EmptyState message='Unable to load data' />;
}

if (data.items.length === 0) {
  return <EmptyState message='No items found' action={{ label: 'Browse All', href: '/listings' }} />;
}
```

Use `src/components/shared/Skeleton.tsx` and `src/components/shared/EmptyState.tsx`.

---

## Step 6 — Animation (optional)

For entrance animations, use `framer-motion` following the pattern in dashboard pages:

```typescript
import { motion } from 'framer-motion';

<motion.div
  initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 20 }}
  animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
  transition={{ delay: index * 0.1 }}>
  <Card>...</Card>
</motion.div>
```

---

## Step 7 — Export and barrel

If the feature directory has an `index.ts` barrel file (like `src/components/reviews/index.ts`), add the new export:

```typescript
export { MyComponent } from './MyComponent';
```

---

## Checklist

- [ ] Component placed in the correct directory (see table in Step 1)
- [ ] `'use client'` only present if hooks/browser APIs are used
- [ ] `cn()` used for all conditional/composable class names
- [ ] Data fetched via `src/hooks/api/` hook (never raw fetch)
- [ ] Loading, error, and empty states handled
- [ ] User feedback uses `sonner` toast (no `alert()`)
- [ ] `npm run typecheck` passes

